1
00:00:11,711 --> 00:00:15,081
How much money does it take to live alone?

2
00:00:16,783 --> 00:00:19,986
Can I live alone on that money?

3
00:00:21,154 --> 00:00:23,289
All of her life insurance money

4
00:00:24,991 --> 00:00:28,395
is proof of her love.

5
00:00:33,266 --> 00:00:37,971
Okay, I got it.
I'm now your personal advisor.

6
00:00:39,773 --> 00:00:43,710
The mountain guide Motoka Tabatake's
life insurance is 30 million yen.

7
00:00:44,411 --> 00:00:49,816
If the cause of death is suicide,
it isn't paid.

8
00:00:52,719 --> 00:00:55,388
I didn't do it.

9
00:00:56,122 --> 00:00:57,390
I didn't.

10
00:00:57,457 --> 00:00:59,659
Do you think Saruwatari really did it?

11
00:01:00,860 --> 00:01:03,797
As long as there's evidence,
we'll consider her a suspect.

12
00:01:04,364 --> 00:01:05,932
It's Ogoma.

13
00:01:05,999 --> 00:01:07,867
Don't admit to what you didn't do.

14
00:01:09,069 --> 00:01:15,508
If the three missing people were alive,
we would know who is telling the truth.

15
00:01:16,643 --> 00:01:17,811
It's Mr. Monden, right?

16
00:01:17,877 --> 00:01:20,980
He's supposed to be missing,
so why is he in Shibuya?

17
00:01:21,047 --> 00:01:22,315
He's alive.

18
00:01:24,684 --> 00:01:26,019
He's a witness.

19
00:01:28,188 --> 00:01:30,256
Doubt everything.

20
00:01:30,323 --> 00:01:34,694
Once you have doubted everything,
what remains is the truth.

21
00:01:37,630 --> 00:01:40,033
-He's really the missing Mr. Monden?
-Good morning.

22
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:41,501
Thank you, and yes.

23
00:01:41,568 --> 00:01:44,304
Huh? If he's safe,
why doesn't he come forward?

24
00:01:44,370 --> 00:01:45,205
Mr. Nao.

25
00:01:45,271 --> 00:01:47,207
Rescue teams are searching
the mountain, right?

26
00:01:47,273 --> 00:01:48,775
Yes, desperately.

27
00:01:48,842 --> 00:01:50,276
What does he do for work?

28
00:01:50,343 --> 00:01:52,212
He's an office worker in Sapporo.

29
00:01:52,278 --> 00:01:53,880
And he came to Tokyo?

30
00:01:54,380 --> 00:01:56,816
He's pretending to be missing?

31
00:01:57,584 --> 00:01:59,419
He doesn't try to go inside.

32
00:01:59,486 --> 00:02:04,324
He wasn't invited, and he may not
have a key to the room.

33
00:02:04,390 --> 00:02:07,293
I'll secure Mr. Monden
and get his side of the story.

34
00:02:07,360 --> 00:02:09,562
What? You plan to look for this man?

35
00:02:09,629 --> 00:02:13,399
Yes. I'll make him tell me
what happened on the mountain.

36
00:02:13,466 --> 00:02:14,434
No…

37
00:02:15,135 --> 00:02:17,937
Who gave Mr. Nikaido the sleeping pill?

38
00:02:20,006 --> 00:02:22,108
What is his relationship with Harune?

39
00:02:22,175 --> 00:02:25,345
Are you sure?
He's not a serial killer, is he?

40
00:02:26,279 --> 00:02:29,916
Could the other two missing people
have been killed on the mountain?

41
00:02:29,983 --> 00:02:31,618
One of them is Mr. Monden's wife.

42
00:02:33,486 --> 00:02:35,155
Husbands, wives, parents, children.

43
00:02:35,221 --> 00:02:36,689
They kill each other all the time.

44
00:02:37,657 --> 00:02:39,392
Generally, they don't.

45
00:02:40,260 --> 00:02:41,861
I'll borrow the residential map.

46
00:02:49,569 --> 00:02:50,270
It's hot!

47
00:02:51,171 --> 00:02:54,941
I think the camera was around here.

48
00:02:56,676 --> 00:02:59,245
-Why is even the shade hot?
-It's summer.

49
00:02:59,312 --> 00:03:01,247
So hot! What is that?

50
00:03:01,915 --> 00:03:03,750
It looks like it's here.

51
00:03:03,816 --> 00:03:06,085
-Right?
-Yes. All right.

52
00:03:06,152 --> 00:03:08,021
-Be careful.
-Yes.

53
00:03:08,087 --> 00:03:10,190
So he's alive…

54
00:03:11,824 --> 00:03:13,426
Coming!

55
00:03:13,493 --> 00:03:15,762
-Excuse me, may I speak with you?
-Hello.

56
00:03:15,828 --> 00:03:17,030
Sure. What is it?

57
00:03:17,096 --> 00:03:20,300
Have you seen the person in this photo?

58
00:03:21,768 --> 00:03:23,002
No, I haven't.

59
00:03:23,069 --> 00:03:24,003
No?

60
00:03:24,070 --> 00:03:27,907
I only work three days a week.
And not at night.

61
00:03:27,974 --> 00:03:30,577
Do you know the man in apartment 206?

62
00:03:30,643 --> 00:03:33,179
The one next to the stairs? Mr. Nikaido?

63
00:03:33,246 --> 00:03:34,380
Yes!

64
00:03:34,447 --> 00:03:37,784
He's from Hokkaido, right?
He once gave me butter candy.

65
00:03:37,850 --> 00:03:38,651
NIKAIDO

66
00:03:38,718 --> 00:03:41,254
When did you last see him?

67
00:03:41,321 --> 00:03:43,256
About a month ago?

68
00:03:43,323 --> 00:03:46,326
He uses the place
when he has work in Tokyo.

69
00:03:46,392 --> 00:03:48,962
What kind of work in Tokyo?

70
00:03:49,028 --> 00:03:51,698
He runs a restaurant, right?
It must be related to that.

71
00:03:51,764 --> 00:03:54,100
May I check the security camera footage?

72
00:03:54,167 --> 00:03:56,035
It's just a fake, you know.

73
00:03:58,938 --> 00:04:01,374
If you remember anything…

74
00:04:01,975 --> 00:04:03,676
-Wait a moment.
-Yes.

75
00:04:03,743 --> 00:04:04,744
Yes?

76
00:04:10,016 --> 00:04:12,585
-What are you even doing?
-Oh, sorry!

77
00:04:12,652 --> 00:04:14,887
That was an accident. Is there anything?

78
00:04:14,954 --> 00:04:17,757
Seriously? Nothing but flyers?

79
00:04:17,824 --> 00:04:19,525
Is there nothing worthwhile?

80
00:04:19,592 --> 00:04:20,526
NIKAIDO

81
00:04:20,593 --> 00:04:22,962
Look, there's something.

82
00:04:23,529 --> 00:04:24,631
What is this?

83
00:04:27,634 --> 00:04:29,202
Excuse me.

84
00:04:29,269 --> 00:04:30,870
Sorry, we're not open for lunch yet.

85
00:04:30,937 --> 00:04:34,907
May I speak with you?
About the people in this photo?

86
00:04:35,675 --> 00:04:37,910
I haven't seen either of them.

87
00:04:39,312 --> 00:04:44,083
This man appeared on your security camera
around 9:00 p.m. two nights ago.

88
00:04:44,817 --> 00:04:46,419
What are you investigating?

89
00:04:46,919 --> 00:04:50,723
Insurance investigation.
There was a car accident near here.

90
00:04:50,790 --> 00:04:52,258
A car accident?

91
00:04:52,325 --> 00:04:53,660
Was there?

92
00:04:53,726 --> 00:04:56,029
-There was!
-No, there…

93
00:04:56,095 --> 00:04:58,464
I don't know,
so please try asking someone else.

94
00:05:02,602 --> 00:05:04,170
What is this?

95
00:05:04,737 --> 00:05:06,406
11 digits…

96
00:05:07,307 --> 00:05:09,342
A product serial number?

97
00:05:09,409 --> 00:05:10,810
Overseas bank code?

98
00:05:10,877 --> 00:05:13,246
But it wouldn't be lined up like this.

99
00:05:13,313 --> 00:05:14,981
Isn't it just a password?

100
00:05:15,048 --> 00:05:16,082
For what?

101
00:05:16,149 --> 00:05:17,150
Wi-Fi.

102
00:05:17,216 --> 00:05:18,818
Why stick it there?

103
00:05:19,319 --> 00:05:20,520
You wouldn't, would you?

104
00:05:21,354 --> 00:05:23,456
Let's look into this too.

105
00:05:23,523 --> 00:05:25,391
What are you going to do now?

106
00:05:25,458 --> 00:05:28,661
Go door to door.
Detectives do the legwork.

107
00:05:30,530 --> 00:05:31,764
That's cool.

108
00:05:31,831 --> 00:05:34,500
-Are you mocking me?
-I'm not.

109
00:05:35,368 --> 00:05:36,936
Will you work with the police?

110
00:05:37,003 --> 00:05:38,471
No way.

111
00:05:39,372 --> 00:05:42,342
If I ask anything,
they'll report back to Hokkaido.

112
00:05:42,408 --> 00:05:45,044
And everything I'm doing
will be reported too.

113
00:05:46,479 --> 00:05:49,248
So we'll investigate
and not tell the police?

114
00:05:49,916 --> 00:05:52,618
I don't know how much
or what they are covering up.

115
00:05:53,486 --> 00:05:55,021
You know what I always say.

116
00:05:55,888 --> 00:05:56,923
Doubt everything?

117
00:05:57,423 --> 00:05:58,858
Tokyo is big, you know?

118
00:05:58,925 --> 00:06:00,026
I know.

119
00:06:00,093 --> 00:06:01,828
Then I'll go

120
00:06:01,894 --> 00:06:06,299
check out the CCTV cameras
and ask if they can give us footage.

121
00:06:11,471 --> 00:06:12,572
All done!

122
00:06:17,543 --> 00:06:18,711
Let's go then.

123
00:06:19,412 --> 00:06:20,246
Let's do it!

124
00:06:38,331 --> 00:06:40,700
Let me confirm again.

125
00:06:42,068 --> 00:06:46,472
Only your fingerprints and
Mr. Nikaido's were found on the bottle.

126
00:06:47,573 --> 00:06:51,811
I'm only telling you what I saw.

127
00:06:51,878 --> 00:06:55,715
The place where you got lost is
on a route no longer used for hiking.

128
00:06:56,716 --> 00:06:57,984
Where were you going?

129
00:06:58,050 --> 00:06:59,685
That's because…

130
00:07:02,722 --> 00:07:04,824
I've told you so many times.

131
00:07:05,658 --> 00:07:07,794
Excuse me! Do you have a moment?

132
00:07:07,860 --> 00:07:08,861
Huh? Police?

133
00:07:08,928 --> 00:07:10,797
No. I'm looking for people…

134
00:07:10,863 --> 00:07:12,131
It's okay.

135
00:07:13,232 --> 00:07:14,634
I'm here.

136
00:07:14,700 --> 00:07:17,336
-If you see them--
-Okay, got it.

137
00:07:17,937 --> 00:07:19,772
Have you seen them anywhere?

138
00:07:19,839 --> 00:07:21,507
No, I haven't.

139
00:07:21,574 --> 00:07:22,742
I don't know.

140
00:07:23,509 --> 00:07:24,343
Come on.

141
00:07:26,312 --> 00:07:28,548
You won't turn into scum.

142
00:07:29,348 --> 00:07:31,851
May I look at the security camera footage?

143
00:07:31,918 --> 00:07:33,152
Who are you?

144
00:07:33,219 --> 00:07:34,821
I'm looking for some people.

145
00:07:34,887 --> 00:07:36,355
We can't show it to civilians.

146
00:07:36,923 --> 00:07:39,258
-Are you police?
-No, I'm not.

147
00:07:39,325 --> 00:07:40,860
Which area are you looking in?

148
00:07:40,927 --> 00:07:42,495
Hold on.

149
00:07:42,562 --> 00:07:43,696
-May I use your map?
-Yes.

150
00:07:43,763 --> 00:07:44,764
Here.

151
00:07:44,831 --> 00:07:45,731
Come on!

152
00:07:45,798 --> 00:07:47,467
-That's too wide!
-Impossible!

153
00:07:47,533 --> 00:07:49,535
You'll need a car to search all of this!

154
00:07:49,602 --> 00:07:50,970
I don't have a car.

155
00:07:51,037 --> 00:07:52,171
A bicycle?

156
00:07:52,238 --> 00:07:53,172
Get a rental one!

157
00:07:53,239 --> 00:07:56,309
Go ahead! Go on through!

158
00:07:56,375 --> 00:08:00,947
Excuse me. If you see them,
please call this number.

159
00:08:01,013 --> 00:08:03,082
-Wait. Show me again.
-Yes?

160
00:08:05,952 --> 00:08:09,422
Would she really throw away 30 million yen
that she could give her daughter?

161
00:08:09,489 --> 00:08:10,423
I love you.

162
00:08:10,490 --> 00:08:12,492
PAID PARKING

163
00:08:12,558 --> 00:08:15,761
Hello. I'm Nao
of Zennichi Insurance Research.

164
00:08:15,828 --> 00:08:19,265
I'm looking for a hit-and-run vehicle.

165
00:08:19,332 --> 00:08:20,766
Welcome, you can sit anywhere.

166
00:08:20,833 --> 00:08:22,335
-Excuse me.
-Yes?

167
00:08:22,401 --> 00:08:25,404
Are those your shop's security cameras?

168
00:08:27,373 --> 00:08:30,343
In Hokkaido, I could cover
the whole town in half a day.

169
00:08:30,843 --> 00:08:33,546
-Will you go back to Hokkaido, then?
-Who said I would go back?

170
00:08:33,613 --> 00:08:36,916
I took leave to come to Tokyo,
so I'm not going back empty-handed.

171
00:08:36,983 --> 00:08:38,518
Did you find anything?

172
00:08:38,584 --> 00:08:40,386
No. But I'm just getting started.

173
00:08:40,453 --> 00:08:42,121
So you found nothing.

174
00:08:42,188 --> 00:08:44,457
Tomorrow, I'll widen the search area.

175
00:08:47,059 --> 00:08:50,363
Mr. Monden lives in Sapporo, right?

176
00:08:51,464 --> 00:08:53,666
He may be staying somewhere.

177
00:08:56,202 --> 00:08:57,436
Where are you staying?

178
00:08:57,503 --> 00:08:59,672
What? Me?

179
00:09:00,373 --> 00:09:01,908
The place I always stay.

180
00:09:04,010 --> 00:09:05,611
Does your place have room?

181
00:09:08,681 --> 00:09:10,550
Haven't you booked a hotel?

182
00:09:10,616 --> 00:09:14,520
It's summer vacation.
All the cheap places are full.

183
00:09:14,587 --> 00:09:18,524
The only available ones cost as much
as rent. Around 30,000 yen a night.

184
00:09:24,530 --> 00:09:28,067
I'll try negotiating to see
if you can stay.

185
00:09:28,134 --> 00:09:29,535
Want to come with me?

186
00:09:29,602 --> 00:09:31,070
NAO

187
00:09:31,137 --> 00:09:31,971
-Hup.
-What?

188
00:09:33,205 --> 00:09:35,474
Is this your home?

189
00:09:35,541 --> 00:09:36,442
Yes.

190
00:09:37,009 --> 00:09:38,711
Don't you work in Hokkaido?

191
00:09:38,778 --> 00:09:40,413
I worked in Tokyo until two years ago.

192
00:09:40,980 --> 00:09:42,982
I hope they haven't changed the lock.

193
00:09:43,049 --> 00:09:45,484
All right, it opened. Come in.

194
00:09:45,551 --> 00:09:46,819
Excuse me.

195
00:09:50,456 --> 00:09:52,592
-Who are you?
-Oh, I'm sorry…

196
00:09:52,658 --> 00:09:54,160
I'm no one suspicious.

197
00:09:54,226 --> 00:09:56,696
I'm home! Go on in.

198
00:09:57,263 --> 00:09:59,498
Are you sure I can stay?

199
00:09:59,565 --> 00:10:00,433
Probably.

200
00:10:00,499 --> 00:10:01,534
Probably?

201
00:10:01,601 --> 00:10:03,269
Did you eat dinner? I bought food.

202
00:10:03,336 --> 00:10:04,370
-Hey!
-What?

203
00:10:04,437 --> 00:10:07,106
Won't I be bothering her? Who is that?

204
00:10:07,173 --> 00:10:08,207
My wife.

205
00:10:09,642 --> 00:10:10,810
Akane.

206
00:10:11,777 --> 00:10:13,179
You're married?

207
00:10:13,245 --> 00:10:14,947
Is that so surprising?

208
00:10:19,218 --> 00:10:20,386
Excuse me.

209
00:10:21,554 --> 00:10:23,122
The food will be ready soon.

210
00:10:23,189 --> 00:10:25,891
A detective from Hokkaido you met at work?

211
00:10:25,958 --> 00:10:27,193
Yes.

212
00:10:28,227 --> 00:10:31,130
She's very cautious,
so show her proof you're trustworthy.

213
00:10:31,197 --> 00:10:32,231
Yes.

214
00:10:36,469 --> 00:10:38,938
I am Ogoma
of the Hokkaido Prefectural Police.

215
00:10:39,005 --> 00:10:39,972
Your police badge?

216
00:10:40,740 --> 00:10:42,808
They can't carry it around on vacation.

217
00:10:42,875 --> 00:10:43,943
Sorry.

218
00:10:47,179 --> 00:10:49,215
I bet you're wondering,
"Is he the real thing?"

219
00:10:50,516 --> 00:10:54,420
People keep asking if I'm impersonating
a cop or running a con.

220
00:10:55,054 --> 00:10:57,957
People from Tokyo are very cautious.

221
00:11:02,228 --> 00:11:04,230
You are on leave, right?

222
00:11:04,296 --> 00:11:05,431
Yes.

223
00:11:05,498 --> 00:11:07,133
I took time off.

224
00:11:08,100 --> 00:11:10,136
And you're still investigating?

225
00:11:10,703 --> 00:11:12,738
He's looking for a witness.

226
00:11:14,206 --> 00:11:16,042
Is it an official investigation?

227
00:11:16,709 --> 00:11:18,444
No, it's an independent one.

228
00:11:19,011 --> 00:11:20,279
Independent?

229
00:11:20,346 --> 00:11:22,615
Don't press him.

230
00:11:22,682 --> 00:11:26,285
He wants to rescue
his benefactor from trouble.

231
00:11:26,352 --> 00:11:29,889
That's also true, but as police,
it's a case I can't ignore.

232
00:11:31,490 --> 00:11:33,392
Then why independently investigate?

233
00:11:33,459 --> 00:11:34,360
Here you go.

234
00:11:34,427 --> 00:11:37,063
You're right to ask that.

235
00:11:37,129 --> 00:11:41,167
It's a long story, so let's eat first.

236
00:11:42,134 --> 00:11:43,969
Okay? All done.

237
00:11:45,738 --> 00:11:47,707
Let's eat.

238
00:11:47,773 --> 00:11:49,341
Thanks for the food.

239
00:11:59,118 --> 00:12:00,386
So good!

240
00:12:00,453 --> 00:12:01,687
It's good.

241
00:12:03,589 --> 00:12:07,860
This meat was on sale too.
It's good meat, right?

242
00:12:07,927 --> 00:12:09,395
It's not bad.

243
00:12:22,408 --> 00:12:24,143
-How is it?
-Average.

244
00:12:25,478 --> 00:12:26,812
Average is best.

245
00:12:29,081 --> 00:12:32,218
I guess I'll use this sauce.

246
00:12:32,284 --> 00:12:35,621
May I ask how you two met?

247
00:12:37,623 --> 00:12:38,791
You really want to know?

248
00:12:40,559 --> 00:12:41,494
Sorry.

249
00:12:47,967 --> 00:12:49,101
Delicious.

250
00:12:55,508 --> 00:12:57,810
Use the house as you like.

251
00:12:57,877 --> 00:12:59,745
I have work tomorrow.

252
00:12:59,812 --> 00:13:01,981
Thank you for letting me stay.

253
00:13:02,047 --> 00:13:02,915
Mr. Nao--

254
00:13:02,982 --> 00:13:05,985
We have been separated for two years.

255
00:13:08,621 --> 00:13:10,956
You shouldn't trust that man too much.

256
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:28,841
What's wrong?

257
00:13:31,177 --> 00:13:34,246
How long has it been
since you last saw your wife?

258
00:13:34,313 --> 00:13:36,782
Huh? A year and…

259
00:13:37,716 --> 00:13:39,185
four months?

260
00:13:41,487 --> 00:13:46,659
If you need to speak with Akane,
I'll stay at an internet café.

261
00:13:46,725 --> 00:13:47,927
Speak to?

262
00:13:47,993 --> 00:13:48,861
Yes.

263
00:13:51,897 --> 00:13:53,065
Not really.

264
00:13:55,034 --> 00:13:56,702
-Really?
-Ogoma, are you married?

265
00:13:56,769 --> 00:13:59,438
I would like to someday.

266
00:13:59,505 --> 00:14:02,374
But no one wants
to live in my remote district.

267
00:14:02,441 --> 00:14:05,010
Maybe find a girlfriend
who loves mountains and nature.

268
00:14:05,077 --> 00:14:08,314
I'll just get promoted to a bigger station
and get out of there.

269
00:14:08,380 --> 00:14:09,815
-Promotion?
-Yes.

270
00:14:10,516 --> 00:14:12,284
-A positive mindset.
-Yes!

271
00:14:12,351 --> 00:14:14,687
Tomorrow will be dangerously hot too.

272
00:14:14,753 --> 00:14:17,189
-So sleep well.
-Yes.

273
00:14:17,256 --> 00:14:19,959
-Okay, good night.
-Good night.

274
00:14:31,136 --> 00:14:32,738
Sorry for worrying you.

275
00:14:32,805 --> 00:14:35,841
And thank you for being on my side.

276
00:15:13,946 --> 00:15:15,080
Good morning.

277
00:15:17,983 --> 00:15:19,351
Where's Ogoma?

278
00:15:20,052 --> 00:15:21,487
He already went out.

279
00:15:23,923 --> 00:15:26,859
Looking for someone in just five days…

280
00:15:27,526 --> 00:15:30,195
It's impossible, but he will try anyway.
That's who he is.

281
00:15:30,930 --> 00:15:34,099
This is the biggest case
of his detective career.

282
00:15:34,166 --> 00:15:37,036
It's complicated, but he must solve it.

283
00:15:42,574 --> 00:15:44,043
How long will you stay?

284
00:15:45,878 --> 00:15:47,413
Could I stay here for a while?

285
00:15:50,883 --> 00:15:53,519
I'll sleep over there.
I'm grabbing a cup of coffee.

286
00:16:06,298 --> 00:16:07,433
Good morning.

287
00:16:07,499 --> 00:16:09,435
Sorry for calling you so early.

288
00:16:09,501 --> 00:16:11,837
It's okay. What's wrong?

289
00:16:11,904 --> 00:16:15,574
It's about my sister's life insurance.

290
00:16:15,641 --> 00:16:17,977
-Did you get the death certificate?
-Yes.

291
00:16:18,043 --> 00:16:21,647
In the "cause of death,"
which box did they tick?

292
00:16:22,982 --> 00:16:24,383
Suicide.

293
00:16:25,451 --> 00:16:29,621
If the cause is suicide,
the insurance won't pay, right?

294
00:16:30,222 --> 00:16:33,092
I would like you to look into something.

295
00:16:35,260 --> 00:16:38,097
About my sister's suicide.

296
00:16:38,163 --> 00:16:42,468
As a family member,
I'm sure you feel that something is off.

297
00:16:43,202 --> 00:16:44,370
Yes.

298
00:16:46,405 --> 00:16:48,507
If I investigate,

299
00:16:48,574 --> 00:16:52,244
I'll need to talk fees and expenses.

300
00:16:53,245 --> 00:16:56,048
How much would I need to pay?

301
00:16:56,615 --> 00:17:00,886
If I prove your sister's death
was not suicide

302
00:17:00,953 --> 00:17:03,655
and the insurance is paid,

303
00:17:03,722 --> 00:17:06,125
I take ten percent as my fee.

304
00:17:08,060 --> 00:17:09,695
Not suicide?

305
00:17:12,264 --> 00:17:13,399
How about it?

306
00:17:13,932 --> 00:17:16,502
I think it's not a bad deal.

307
00:17:19,571 --> 00:17:21,640
Have you seen these people?

308
00:17:22,474 --> 00:17:23,475
Take care.

309
00:17:24,376 --> 00:17:25,744
Let me check.

310
00:17:25,811 --> 00:17:27,212
You can't sit here!

311
00:17:28,747 --> 00:17:29,948
Don't you have school?

312
00:17:30,449 --> 00:17:31,583
Thank you.

313
00:17:31,650 --> 00:17:32,985
Take care.

314
00:17:37,790 --> 00:17:41,527
I may have seen them,
they have been staying several nights.

315
00:17:41,593 --> 00:17:43,662
-Excuse me. I'm opening the door.
-Okay.

316
00:17:45,164 --> 00:17:46,665
What is it?

317
00:17:47,466 --> 00:17:49,168
You don't look similar at all. Sorry.

318
00:17:49,234 --> 00:17:52,404
"13@…"

319
00:17:52,471 --> 00:17:53,539
Hey.

320
00:17:53,605 --> 00:17:55,641
I'm looking for some people.

321
00:17:55,707 --> 00:17:57,076
Have you seen them?

322
00:17:57,142 --> 00:17:58,444
We don't know.

323
00:17:58,510 --> 00:17:59,711
Is this a scam?

324
00:17:59,778 --> 00:18:01,780
-It's not!
-You're scary.

325
00:18:01,847 --> 00:18:03,449
How am I scary?

326
00:18:04,349 --> 00:18:06,185
Excuse me. Have you seen these people?

327
00:18:06,251 --> 00:18:07,419
-No?
-No clue.

328
00:18:07,486 --> 00:18:08,153
You don't know?

329
00:18:08,220 --> 00:18:08,887
I guess not.

330
00:18:08,954 --> 00:18:11,390
Have you seen these people?

331
00:18:11,457 --> 00:18:12,624
I haven't.

332
00:18:12,691 --> 00:18:13,926
Anyone who looks similar?

333
00:18:13,992 --> 00:18:14,927
Hello.

334
00:18:14,993 --> 00:18:17,763
Have you seen these people?

335
00:18:22,334 --> 00:18:25,104
We close at 8:00 p.m., understood?

336
00:18:39,418 --> 00:18:43,355
I'M TAKAHASHI FROM THE CONSTRUCTION SITE
I FOUND SOMEONE WHO HAS SEEN THEM!

337
00:18:43,422 --> 00:18:45,090
Yes!

338
00:18:45,157 --> 00:18:47,092
We close at 8:00 p.m.!

339
00:18:47,159 --> 00:18:48,927
-Hurry up and eat!
-Okay.

340
00:18:50,329 --> 00:18:51,663
I got a lead!

341
00:18:51,730 --> 00:18:54,333
I was contacted about someone
having seen Mr. Monden!

342
00:18:54,399 --> 00:18:57,302
A construction worker shared
the photos in a group chat.

343
00:18:57,369 --> 00:19:00,873
A group chat with 170 people!
Is that normal in Tokyo? Isn't that crazy?

344
00:19:01,473 --> 00:19:03,542
-I'll make room.
-Hey!

345
00:19:03,609 --> 00:19:05,544
You're being a bit rough.

346
00:19:05,611 --> 00:19:06,945
Sorry.

347
00:19:09,748 --> 00:19:11,083
It's here.

348
00:19:11,150 --> 00:19:14,186
The traffic guide who stood here
on the night of August 4th

349
00:19:14,253 --> 00:19:17,122
remembered stopping Mr. Monden's car.

350
00:19:17,189 --> 00:19:19,825
-There is construction ahead.
-I have to turn around?

351
00:19:19,892 --> 00:19:21,560
-A car?
-Yes, a car.

352
00:19:22,728 --> 00:19:27,266
To detour to Mr. Nikaido's condo,
he needs to take this route.

353
00:19:27,332 --> 00:19:29,134
When the CCTV caught him, he was walking.

354
00:19:29,201 --> 00:19:30,102
Which means…

355
00:19:30,169 --> 00:19:31,937
He must have parked somewhere!

356
00:19:32,004 --> 00:19:34,640
If we know the plate number,
we can trace the owner's contact.

357
00:19:34,706 --> 00:19:35,541
Car model?

358
00:19:35,607 --> 00:19:38,877
Unknown, but it's a white sedan.
Do you have the camera footage there?

359
00:19:38,944 --> 00:19:40,779
More or less.

360
00:19:40,846 --> 00:19:43,182
Let's find this car! Bring it on!

361
00:19:43,248 --> 00:19:44,550
We're getting closer!

362
00:19:46,852 --> 00:19:49,855
Have something to drink and take a break.

363
00:19:51,023 --> 00:19:52,024
Okay.

364
00:19:54,560 --> 00:19:57,262
Did you figure out the meaning
behind those 11 digits?

365
00:19:57,329 --> 00:19:59,131
Not at all.

366
00:19:59,198 --> 00:20:04,303
I think only Mr. Nikaido knows.

367
00:20:12,177 --> 00:20:13,111
Here.

368
00:20:13,879 --> 00:20:14,780
Thank you.

369
00:20:15,480 --> 00:20:19,918
So many things we don't know.

370
00:20:33,732 --> 00:20:34,833
Good morning.

371
00:20:39,037 --> 00:20:40,739
Should I move from here?

372
00:20:41,506 --> 00:20:42,774
Where is he?

373
00:20:44,076 --> 00:20:47,379
Mr. Nao went to collect
security camera footage.

374
00:20:47,446 --> 00:20:49,514
We found a lead yesterday.

375
00:20:51,216 --> 00:20:52,618
Would you like some?

376
00:20:52,684 --> 00:20:54,653
Yes! Thank you.

377
00:20:57,623 --> 00:21:00,158
Did you walk around all day yesterday?

378
00:21:00,859 --> 00:21:02,494
Aren't you tired?

379
00:21:02,561 --> 00:21:04,162
I prefer moving around.

380
00:21:04,229 --> 00:21:07,332
It makes me feel
like a police detective. I love it.

381
00:21:09,234 --> 00:21:11,003
Do you not get to do it often?

382
00:21:12,704 --> 00:21:15,474
My district has a small population.

383
00:21:15,540 --> 00:21:19,411
When a crime happens,
oftentimes, I instantly know who did it.

384
00:21:19,478 --> 00:21:21,513
It's not even worth searching.

385
00:21:26,418 --> 00:21:29,621
You know him through work, right?

386
00:21:32,357 --> 00:21:36,428
Actually, I only met him last week.

387
00:21:40,465 --> 00:21:41,967
Do you trust him?

388
00:21:46,171 --> 00:21:51,510
Honestly, at first I thought,
"What a nonchalant guy."

389
00:21:51,576 --> 00:21:53,211
I was the opposite.

390
00:21:54,279 --> 00:21:58,183
I met him in a night class at university.

391
00:21:59,251 --> 00:22:02,321
I worked at the same
insurance company he's at now.

392
00:22:03,722 --> 00:22:05,957
Sorry, what are we talking about?

393
00:22:07,426 --> 00:22:09,161
You wanted to know how I met him, right?

394
00:22:09,227 --> 00:22:10,495
Yes! That's me.

395
00:22:10,562 --> 00:22:13,098
Sorry. Please continue.

396
00:22:15,133 --> 00:22:16,535
After work,

397
00:22:17,969 --> 00:22:23,108
he and I both studied
risk management at university.

398
00:22:25,811 --> 00:22:29,848
He was knowledgeable,
quick-witted, and confident.

399
00:22:29,915 --> 00:22:32,150
I thought he was trustworthy.

400
00:22:32,217 --> 00:22:35,020
I'm beginning to think so too.

401
00:22:35,987 --> 00:22:37,122
Am I wrong?

402
00:22:38,657 --> 00:22:39,925
Now,

403
00:22:41,493 --> 00:22:45,130
when I see his face, I think…

404
00:22:46,531 --> 00:22:49,735
"What a nonchalant guy."

405
00:22:51,136 --> 00:22:52,537
He's like that.

406
00:22:52,604 --> 00:22:54,706
He doesn't care which method he uses.

407
00:22:55,407 --> 00:22:59,478
But I feel like no matter what,
he will find out the truth.

408
00:22:59,544 --> 00:23:00,746
So I trust him.

409
00:23:09,020 --> 00:23:10,155
Shall I help?

410
00:23:10,222 --> 00:23:11,723
With what?

411
00:23:11,790 --> 00:23:13,859
With what you're doing now.

412
00:23:13,925 --> 00:23:16,261
What?! Are you sure?

413
00:23:16,795 --> 00:23:20,031
But, don't you have work?

414
00:23:20,098 --> 00:23:23,435
I'm on summer vacation starting today.
What should I look for?

415
00:23:24,703 --> 00:23:26,505
Then, thank you.

416
00:23:27,406 --> 00:23:29,341
I need your help to find a white car.

417
00:23:29,408 --> 00:23:30,242
Okay.

418
00:23:30,308 --> 00:23:31,376
It looks delicious!

419
00:23:35,514 --> 00:23:38,350
You aren't going anywhere
for summer vacation?

420
00:23:39,351 --> 00:23:41,052
Everywhere is crowded.

421
00:23:42,020 --> 00:23:44,022
Too many people, yes.

422
00:23:44,089 --> 00:23:46,792
I want to go somewhere without people.

423
00:23:47,959 --> 00:23:49,261
Thank you for the food.

424
00:23:49,327 --> 00:23:51,463
I wonder what place
isn't crowded these days.

425
00:23:53,799 --> 00:23:57,569
When my daughter was alive,
we climbed mountains every year.

426
00:24:04,176 --> 00:24:06,812
Did he not tell you about our daughter?

427
00:24:08,680 --> 00:24:09,514
No.

428
00:24:14,986 --> 00:24:16,521
She died.

429
00:24:19,257 --> 00:24:20,592
She was six.

430
00:24:25,330 --> 00:24:28,800
That man just kept on blaming…

431
00:24:30,001 --> 00:24:31,169
himself.

432
00:24:38,944 --> 00:24:41,780
How is it going?
Did you find the white sedan?

433
00:24:41,847 --> 00:24:44,483
It didn't appear in any parking lot.

434
00:24:44,549 --> 00:24:47,352
Is that even possible?

435
00:24:47,419 --> 00:24:49,287
Maybe they parked on the street?

436
00:24:49,354 --> 00:24:50,722
The search would never end.

437
00:24:51,356 --> 00:24:54,392
Maybe we should officially ask the police.

438
00:24:54,459 --> 00:24:56,394
Large-scale searches are their strength.

439
00:24:56,461 --> 00:24:58,630
I will find it tomorrow, no matter what!

440
00:25:01,433 --> 00:25:02,467
Hey, Ogoma.

441
00:25:03,101 --> 00:25:04,669
Can you come here now?

442
00:25:05,570 --> 00:25:08,106
I'm going to talk to Nono…

443
00:25:09,107 --> 00:25:10,775
about Ms. Tabatake.

444
00:25:10,842 --> 00:25:12,277
You should join me.

445
00:25:12,911 --> 00:25:13,812
Okay.

446
00:25:17,516 --> 00:25:19,584
Nono, can you hear us?

447
00:25:20,652 --> 00:25:24,356
Can I have
this policeman listen in on us too?

448
00:25:26,024 --> 00:25:27,626
Hello.

449
00:25:27,692 --> 00:25:28,927
Hello.

450
00:25:28,994 --> 00:25:31,196
Look, this is the sky in Tokyo!

451
00:25:33,064 --> 00:25:36,902
Let's get to the point.

452
00:25:38,136 --> 00:25:42,407
Last time, there was something
you couldn't say about your mom, right?

453
00:25:42,474 --> 00:25:43,909
Nono.

454
00:25:44,976 --> 00:25:48,880
Is it about what you mentioned to me
at the hospital last time?

455
00:25:48,947 --> 00:25:50,248
Was my Mommy…

456
00:25:51,449 --> 00:25:53,184
killed?

457
00:25:59,758 --> 00:26:05,163
Can you tell us why you think that?

458
00:26:05,230 --> 00:26:06,765
Any reason is fine.

459
00:26:06,831 --> 00:26:09,534
We want to know
what your Mom was thinking.

460
00:26:12,771 --> 00:26:13,838
Mommy…

461
00:26:14,906 --> 00:26:19,177
was always worried someone
would come to our house.

462
00:26:20,145 --> 00:26:23,248
When there was a noise outside,
she went to check right away.

463
00:26:23,315 --> 00:26:24,950
Did someone come?

464
00:26:26,217 --> 00:26:27,686
No, there was no one.

465
00:26:29,888 --> 00:26:30,989
-Is it this?
-Yeah.

466
00:26:32,657 --> 00:26:34,392
Then, I'll make a star.

467
00:26:35,760 --> 00:26:39,564
She told me never to follow strangers,
even if they spoke to me.

468
00:26:39,631 --> 00:26:41,399
She said it to me again and again.

469
00:26:41,466 --> 00:26:43,602
-You good? Okay.
-I'm going!

470
00:26:46,871 --> 00:26:48,440
-I'm late!
-Take care!

471
00:26:48,506 --> 00:26:49,574
Bye!

472
00:27:00,485 --> 00:27:02,687
What do you mean I can't turn back now?

473
00:27:06,524 --> 00:27:07,892
I'll call you back.

474
00:27:07,959 --> 00:27:10,328
Was she always like that?

475
00:27:10,395 --> 00:27:11,963
No.

476
00:27:12,030 --> 00:27:12,998
Welcome home.

477
00:27:13,064 --> 00:27:16,568
When did your Mom start acting scared?

478
00:27:16,635 --> 00:27:18,937
In the last few months, apparently.

479
00:27:19,004 --> 00:27:23,775
And a while before that,
she told me she got a new job.

480
00:27:23,842 --> 00:27:26,277
Aside from being a mountain guide
and a driver?

481
00:27:26,344 --> 00:27:27,178
Yes.

482
00:27:27,245 --> 00:27:29,648
I told her not to overwork,

483
00:27:30,448 --> 00:27:34,552
but she said this job
doesn't take much time and pays well.

484
00:27:34,619 --> 00:27:38,456
Nono, did she ever tell you
what the job was?

485
00:27:42,861 --> 00:27:45,130
I also don't know much.

486
00:27:47,599 --> 00:27:49,901
I'll look into that.

487
00:27:49,968 --> 00:27:51,069
Can you?

488
00:27:51,136 --> 00:27:54,139
Of course. Who do you think I am?

489
00:27:57,208 --> 00:27:58,710
-Chika.
-Yes?

490
00:27:58,777 --> 00:28:01,312
May I ask a favor?

491
00:28:01,379 --> 00:28:02,347
Sure.

492
00:28:02,414 --> 00:28:03,915
Nono, don't worry.

493
00:28:04,549 --> 00:28:06,985
There's nothing to worry about.

494
00:28:07,052 --> 00:28:07,986
Okay.

495
00:28:10,021 --> 00:28:12,457
Huh? Tabatake's jobs?

496
00:28:13,091 --> 00:28:14,659
She was a guide and driver, right?

497
00:28:14,726 --> 00:28:16,861
Did she have another job?

498
00:28:16,928 --> 00:28:18,930
Part-time or short-term?

499
00:28:18,997 --> 00:28:20,265
How long is your vacation?

500
00:28:21,700 --> 00:28:23,134
Until tomorrow.

501
00:28:23,201 --> 00:28:24,536
Make sure you come back.

502
00:28:25,704 --> 00:28:27,238
Saruwatari is about to confess…

503
00:28:27,305 --> 00:28:29,874
She was interrogated
for eight days straight.

504
00:28:29,941 --> 00:28:31,543
She's nearing her limit.

505
00:28:37,949 --> 00:28:40,585
I can ask the police to let you rest.

506
00:28:40,652 --> 00:28:44,355
No. If I refuse,
I'll look more suspicious.

507
00:28:44,422 --> 00:28:46,758
It doesn't matter.
It's just voluntary questioning.

508
00:28:48,193 --> 00:28:51,062
Please put your health first.

509
00:28:52,230 --> 00:28:53,198
Yes.

510
00:28:54,599 --> 00:28:56,401
Hello?

511
00:28:57,135 --> 00:28:59,003
How have you been?

512
00:29:00,038 --> 00:29:02,574
How are your injuries?
How is the investigation going?

513
00:29:03,608 --> 00:29:07,278
I know it's their job,
but the police sure are persistent, right?

514
00:29:10,782 --> 00:29:15,620
How can I make them believe what I say?

515
00:29:17,455 --> 00:29:18,590
The police

516
00:29:20,058 --> 00:29:23,394
are investigating under
the assumption you're the culprit.

517
00:29:23,895 --> 00:29:26,698
They haven't arrested you
for questioning yet, right?

518
00:29:26,765 --> 00:29:28,566
Arrested?

519
00:29:29,768 --> 00:29:33,471
If you say anything that sounds
even slightly like admitting guilt,

520
00:29:33,538 --> 00:29:35,106
they'll switch to it.

521
00:29:36,374 --> 00:29:38,343
Even though I did nothing?

522
00:29:38,409 --> 00:29:41,713
Ogoma is working hard every day for you.

523
00:29:41,780 --> 00:29:43,047
Don't forget that.

524
00:29:48,086 --> 00:29:50,421
Can you tell Ogoma something for me?

525
00:29:52,056 --> 00:29:56,127
That as long as I have even one ally,
I can bear it.

526
00:30:00,031 --> 00:30:01,432
I'll tell him.

527
00:30:02,534 --> 00:30:05,270
We're always here to talk,
both me and Ogoma.

528
00:30:08,673 --> 00:30:10,341
Thank you.

529
00:30:12,777 --> 00:30:14,612
-Are you going somewhere?
-Yes.

530
00:30:14,679 --> 00:30:18,383
I'm going to check the parking lots
around Mr. Nikaido's condo again.

531
00:30:18,449 --> 00:30:19,617
Hold on. I got it.

532
00:30:19,684 --> 00:30:21,152
-Hold on.
-But why?

533
00:30:21,219 --> 00:30:23,655
-I have to go! I have no time!
-It's okay. Come on.

534
00:30:24,556 --> 00:30:25,924
Just stay here for now.

535
00:30:25,990 --> 00:30:27,091
I have no time.

536
00:30:27,158 --> 00:30:29,127
Leave going outside until tomorrow.

537
00:30:30,562 --> 00:30:33,064
Is Harune really in Tokyo?

538
00:30:33,131 --> 00:30:34,899
She definitely took a plane
bound for Haneda.

539
00:30:35,466 --> 00:30:39,137
My sister, Harune,
left her medicine at home.

540
00:30:39,204 --> 00:30:40,038
Yes?

541
00:30:40,104 --> 00:30:42,974
But she's on airplane mode,
so I can't reach her.

542
00:30:43,041 --> 00:30:43,942
Okay.

543
00:30:44,008 --> 00:30:45,210
Without it,

544
00:30:46,444 --> 00:30:47,478
she'll die!

545
00:30:47,545 --> 00:30:50,481
You keep making up
the most outrageous lies.

546
00:30:50,548 --> 00:30:53,184
-Police do it often.
-I've never done it.

547
00:30:53,251 --> 00:30:54,519
Nor will you?

548
00:30:54,586 --> 00:30:56,487
As a rule, I don't want to.

549
00:30:56,554 --> 00:30:58,423
Flexibility is important these days.

550
00:30:58,489 --> 00:31:00,692
-You're just saying whatever.
-Ogoma.

551
00:31:01,426 --> 00:31:03,094
Have you contacted Ms. Aya?

552
00:31:03,695 --> 00:31:05,129
-I haven't.
-Why? Do it!

553
00:31:05,196 --> 00:31:08,299
I'll get evidence, then come back
to Hokkaido and call her.

554
00:31:08,366 --> 00:31:09,467
So let me go.

555
00:31:09,534 --> 00:31:13,471
By the way, isn't this bed too small?

556
00:31:15,139 --> 00:31:17,208
It's fine.

557
00:31:17,275 --> 00:31:19,310
It's definitely too small!

558
00:31:20,945 --> 00:31:27,051
Akane is a capable person,
but sometimes she misses things like this.

559
00:31:28,319 --> 00:31:30,421
This is definitely too small. Let me--

560
00:31:31,089 --> 00:31:32,490
-What?
-This room…

561
00:31:33,424 --> 00:31:35,326
This is your daughter's room, right?

562
00:31:42,834 --> 00:31:44,535
Did she like stars?

563
00:31:49,908 --> 00:31:50,875
Yes.

564
00:31:54,946 --> 00:31:56,881
Did Akane tell you something?

565
00:31:58,349 --> 00:32:00,385
Yes, a little.

566
00:32:00,451 --> 00:32:01,486
What did she say?

567
00:32:02,420 --> 00:32:04,255
That it was a traffic accident.

568
00:32:05,290 --> 00:32:06,658
That's about it.

569
00:32:11,896 --> 00:32:13,765
It was right after she entered
elementary school.

570
00:32:16,401 --> 00:32:17,535
Dad!

571
00:32:18,736 --> 00:32:24,943
I had that day off,
so I went to her school to see her.

572
00:32:29,147 --> 00:32:31,516
You must think
I'm an overprotective parent.

573
00:32:31,582 --> 00:32:32,483
No.

574
00:32:33,318 --> 00:32:36,554
She was in nursery school up until then,

575
00:32:36,621 --> 00:32:39,624
and either Akane
or I still had to pick her up,

576
00:32:39,691 --> 00:32:41,292
so I was just worried.

577
00:33:14,926 --> 00:33:17,095
I called an ambulance right away.

578
00:33:18,029 --> 00:33:20,965
But she didn't make it.

579
00:33:22,367 --> 00:33:23,868
Hey, turn her over here.

580
00:33:27,405 --> 00:33:29,474
-Decide!
-Which one do you want to stick up?

581
00:33:29,540 --> 00:33:32,010
This one? Oh, this one?

582
00:33:32,076 --> 00:33:33,644
Okay, here you go.

583
00:33:43,755 --> 00:33:47,825
You probably feel the same.

584
00:33:49,994 --> 00:33:56,200
Why is it so hard to part with someone
who is no longer in this world?

585
00:33:58,336 --> 00:34:01,339
They're always…

586
00:34:01,906 --> 00:34:04,042
on your mind, right?

587
00:34:07,812 --> 00:34:08,980
Thank you.

588
00:34:09,547 --> 00:34:10,415
Hot!

589
00:34:11,315 --> 00:34:12,517
Yes.

590
00:34:13,284 --> 00:34:14,786
It's strange, isn't it?

591
00:34:17,455 --> 00:34:19,791
Wait!

592
00:34:23,961 --> 00:34:24,796
There!

593
00:34:24,862 --> 00:34:28,099
-Whoa!
-Nice! Stick them on harder!

594
00:34:49,153 --> 00:34:51,055
Was there a parking lot over here?

595
00:34:51,122 --> 00:34:53,357
Your residential map is old.

596
00:34:53,424 --> 00:34:55,827
This place became an empty lot
and then a parking lot.

597
00:34:56,661 --> 00:34:58,329
You did great finding it.

598
00:34:58,396 --> 00:35:00,998
All that walking around paid off.

599
00:35:01,732 --> 00:35:02,633
This is the place.

600
00:35:02,700 --> 00:35:05,036
-Nice.
-What do you mean "nice"?

601
00:35:06,838 --> 00:35:07,939
Thank you.

602
00:35:09,107 --> 00:35:10,141
Welcome.

603
00:35:11,142 --> 00:35:12,176
You again.

604
00:35:12,243 --> 00:35:13,478
Hello.

605
00:35:13,544 --> 00:35:16,080
I would like to ask
about the night of August 4th.

606
00:35:16,147 --> 00:35:18,483
I'm busy. Ask someone else.

607
00:35:18,549 --> 00:35:20,318
Please! Can you listen to me?

608
00:35:20,384 --> 00:35:22,653
-The "car accident" was a lie, right?
-It was, sorry.

609
00:35:23,588 --> 00:35:25,690
You were lying too.

610
00:35:25,756 --> 00:35:28,593
I showed many people those photos.

611
00:35:28,659 --> 00:35:33,564
Most took a long look at them,
and tried to jog their memory.

612
00:35:33,631 --> 00:35:36,501
But only you said,
"I haven't seen them," right away.

613
00:35:36,567 --> 00:35:38,803
I haven't seen either of them.

614
00:35:39,537 --> 00:35:42,240
I'm Ogoma, with Hokkaido Police.

615
00:35:42,306 --> 00:35:45,743
I'm Nao from Zennichi Insurance Research.

616
00:35:46,978 --> 00:35:48,012
Take care.

617
00:35:49,280 --> 00:35:52,850
On the night of August 4th,
this man talked to me.

618
00:35:52,917 --> 00:35:55,052
He said he was looking for this woman.

619
00:35:55,119 --> 00:35:56,721
Looking for her?

620
00:35:57,955 --> 00:36:01,259
What about that car
parked in the lot behind?

621
00:36:01,325 --> 00:36:02,460
It's mine.

622
00:36:03,027 --> 00:36:08,166
August 4th at 9:00 p.m.

623
00:36:08,866 --> 00:36:13,171
He gave me 10,000 yen
and asked me not to tell anyone.

624
00:36:15,339 --> 00:36:17,108
-Quite visible.
-Yes.

625
00:36:17,175 --> 00:36:18,943
-Can you stop it here?
-Yes.

626
00:36:19,010 --> 00:36:20,311
I can see the plate numbers!

627
00:36:20,378 --> 00:36:21,712
Yes! Thank you so much!

628
00:36:21,779 --> 00:36:23,114
I love you!

629
00:36:23,181 --> 00:36:24,348
Come on!

630
00:36:24,415 --> 00:36:26,884
-Do you have his contact information?
-You do, right?

631
00:36:26,951 --> 00:36:27,885
Yes!

632
00:36:27,952 --> 00:36:29,687
All right!

633
00:36:29,754 --> 00:36:32,390
-Who are you calling?
-070… Huh? This number.

634
00:36:32,456 --> 00:36:33,524
Why are you calling?

635
00:36:33,591 --> 00:36:36,093
-I'll call him over. Oh, come on!
-No!

636
00:36:36,160 --> 00:36:38,930
You need more information first.
Are you stupid?

637
00:36:38,996 --> 00:36:40,464
A plate check?

638
00:36:40,531 --> 00:36:43,668
Yes, here's the plate number.
Shinagawa 301…

639
00:36:43,734 --> 00:36:45,203
What are you doing?

640
00:36:45,836 --> 00:36:47,138
Nothing.

641
00:36:47,205 --> 00:36:49,574
Don't tell me
you're sneakily investigating?

642
00:36:49,640 --> 00:36:51,309
I am not…

643
00:36:51,375 --> 00:36:53,511
Why do you sound so unsure?

644
00:36:53,578 --> 00:36:56,981
I told you, we're officers!
Just follow the higher-ups!

645
00:36:58,115 --> 00:36:59,517
Here.

646
00:36:59,584 --> 00:37:00,484
Wait a moment.

647
00:37:00,551 --> 00:37:02,053
An officer from Hokkaido?

648
00:37:02,119 --> 00:37:03,754
He's investigating something.

649
00:37:06,224 --> 00:37:09,093
I'm Tamura
from Yoyogi Central Police Station.

650
00:37:09,660 --> 00:37:12,430
A person from your station is here.

651
00:37:12,964 --> 00:37:13,965
Yes.

652
00:37:14,031 --> 00:37:15,733
I told you not to act on your own!

653
00:37:17,034 --> 00:37:17,969
Sorry.

654
00:37:18,035 --> 00:37:19,704
When you come back, report everything.

655
00:37:20,404 --> 00:37:21,606
Don't come empty-handed.

656
00:37:22,340 --> 00:37:23,641
Did something happen?

657
00:37:23,708 --> 00:37:24,909
No, nothing.

658
00:37:26,110 --> 00:37:27,211
Hello, sir!

659
00:37:27,278 --> 00:37:28,112
Good work today.

660
00:37:28,179 --> 00:37:29,113
Thank you.

661
00:37:29,180 --> 00:37:30,648
Shirokuma Car Lease?

662
00:37:30,715 --> 00:37:32,850
Shall I ask the lease company?

663
00:37:34,485 --> 00:37:37,321
No. Call Mr. Monden.

664
00:37:41,158 --> 00:37:42,093
Hello.

665
00:37:42,627 --> 00:37:46,364
Um… Hello? I am…

666
00:37:47,732 --> 00:37:49,934
I'm sorry to bother you.

667
00:37:50,001 --> 00:37:53,137
I'm Suzuki from Shirokuma Car Lease.

668
00:37:53,204 --> 00:37:57,308
We have an urgent notice
about the vehicle you're using.

669
00:37:58,309 --> 00:37:59,210
What?

670
00:37:59,277 --> 00:38:02,179
We found parts in it that need replacing.

671
00:38:02,246 --> 00:38:03,447
So for your safety,

672
00:38:03,514 --> 00:38:06,884
we must ask you to swap
to a substitute vehicle right away.

673
00:38:06,951 --> 00:38:07,952
Today?

674
00:38:08,019 --> 00:38:11,689
Yes. I'm really sorry to bother you!
When would you be available?

675
00:38:17,862 --> 00:38:19,730
Will Mr. Monden really come?

676
00:38:19,797 --> 00:38:22,099
I don't know.

677
00:38:30,675 --> 00:38:33,678
I have something to tell you.

678
00:38:34,345 --> 00:38:38,916
Chika gave me some documents
on Ms. Tabatake's household finances.

679
00:38:40,518 --> 00:38:43,654
Bank accounts, credit card statements,
and so on.

680
00:38:44,588 --> 00:38:48,159
Wages for the guide
and driver jobs are deposited there.

681
00:38:48,225 --> 00:38:52,930
But no deposits for the other job
Nono mentioned.

682
00:38:53,497 --> 00:38:56,334
So it's paid in cash?

683
00:38:56,400 --> 00:38:58,636
Do you know how much
Nono's treatment costs?

684
00:38:59,637 --> 00:39:01,572
I can't tell from the bank account.

685
00:39:01,639 --> 00:39:04,141
But look at this.

686
00:39:04,208 --> 00:39:06,444
We can roughly see Nono's medical costs.

687
00:39:07,111 --> 00:39:07,778
What?

688
00:39:07,845 --> 00:39:10,715
Nono's illness is covered
by insurance, right?

689
00:39:10,781 --> 00:39:13,217
It shouldn't cost this much.
This is astronomical.

690
00:39:14,185 --> 00:39:17,655
Maybe she was prescribed drugs
not covered by insurance.

691
00:39:18,322 --> 00:39:21,692
It's roughly one million yen per month.

692
00:39:21,759 --> 00:39:24,495
The math doesn't add up.

693
00:39:25,396 --> 00:39:28,866
Even working as a guide and driver,
she cannot cover all of that.

694
00:39:30,634 --> 00:39:34,071
A super well-paying job
that pays solely in cash…

695
00:39:34,138 --> 00:39:36,707
As a police officer,
I can only think of one thing.

696
00:39:38,142 --> 00:39:39,577
Crime.

697
00:39:40,411 --> 00:39:43,481
If even I can figure it out,
the police must have a clue, right?

698
00:39:43,547 --> 00:39:44,782
They didn't tell you?

699
00:39:44,849 --> 00:39:48,419
They never told me. That's why I'm here.

700
00:39:48,486 --> 00:39:50,488
Will Nono be okay?

701
00:39:50,554 --> 00:39:53,624
If she can't afford
those medical costs anymore…

702
00:39:53,691 --> 00:39:57,595
I won't let that happen.
I will make sure she is okay.

703
00:40:06,470 --> 00:40:07,505
Why are you grinning?

704
00:40:07,571 --> 00:40:09,473
Shirokuma Car Lease!

705
00:40:09,540 --> 00:40:11,675
Sorry for the trouble.

706
00:40:15,980 --> 00:40:17,081
Hey!

707
00:40:18,215 --> 00:40:19,550
-Wait!
-Hey!

708
00:40:19,617 --> 00:40:20,551
Wait!

709
00:40:20,618 --> 00:40:21,886
Why are you running?

710
00:40:21,952 --> 00:40:23,554
-Hey!
-Hold on!

711
00:40:23,621 --> 00:40:25,589
Why are you running?!

712
00:40:25,656 --> 00:40:27,425
Stop!

713
00:40:29,627 --> 00:40:31,328
Monden!

714
00:40:32,363 --> 00:40:34,265
Ogoma!

715
00:40:43,374 --> 00:40:45,075
Which way?

716
00:40:45,142 --> 00:40:46,277
This way!

717
00:40:47,478 --> 00:40:49,980
This way, I guess.

718
00:40:50,047 --> 00:40:51,282
Wait!

719
00:40:54,185 --> 00:40:55,453
Wait!

720
00:40:56,487 --> 00:40:57,855
Stop right there!

721
00:40:57,922 --> 00:41:00,691
EMERGENCY EXIT

722
00:41:02,960 --> 00:41:04,195
Not that way.

723
00:41:05,029 --> 00:41:05,863
Hey!

724
00:41:05,930 --> 00:41:08,732
I'm telling you! Stop!

725
00:41:08,799 --> 00:41:11,135
Where?

726
00:41:14,305 --> 00:41:16,941
Got him! Ogoma, I got him!

727
00:41:17,007 --> 00:41:18,509
It hurts!

728
00:41:18,576 --> 00:41:19,844
Wait!

729
00:41:30,387 --> 00:41:31,922
Okay, okay!

730
00:41:32,456 --> 00:41:34,592
I give up!

731
00:41:35,125 --> 00:41:36,794
Get your dirty hands off him!

732
00:41:38,963 --> 00:41:39,830
Sorry!

733
00:41:39,897 --> 00:41:42,132
-What're you doing?!
-Bring it on!

734
00:41:45,269 --> 00:41:46,036
It hurts!

735
00:41:48,472 --> 00:41:50,808
Here we go again! Stop!

736
00:41:55,713 --> 00:41:57,381
What? Who are you?

737
00:41:57,448 --> 00:41:59,049
As if I'd tell you, idiot.

738
00:42:04,889 --> 00:42:06,490
Just give up already!

739
00:42:18,235 --> 00:42:21,472
Amateur! If you don't hold back, I'll die!

740
00:42:21,539 --> 00:42:22,806
You're the idiot here!

741
00:42:29,680 --> 00:42:32,449
I know who you are. Got it?

742
00:42:39,857 --> 00:42:41,959
You're Ryutaro Monden, right?

743
00:42:43,594 --> 00:42:45,029
I bet you want to know who I am.

744
00:42:50,534 --> 00:42:51,702
Follow me.

745
00:43:04,214 --> 00:43:06,517
Don't tell anyone
what I'm about to tell you.

746
00:43:06,584 --> 00:43:07,952
I'll think about it.

747
00:43:08,018 --> 00:43:09,420
Don't be cocky.

748
00:43:41,418 --> 00:43:43,754
Can you tell me your story?

749
00:43:46,957 --> 00:43:48,759
The security camera footage with me on it…

750
00:43:53,163 --> 00:43:54,498
Who in the police…

751
00:43:55,332 --> 00:43:56,634
has seen it?

752
00:43:58,802 --> 00:44:01,071
I don't know what happened
on that mountain…

753
00:44:01,138 --> 00:44:02,873
How will you take responsibility?

754
00:44:02,940 --> 00:44:04,742
We have to admit it failed.

755
00:44:04,808 --> 00:44:07,311
Can you keep this a secret?

756
00:44:07,978 --> 00:44:08,946
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
